m(Vᵢ), Aᵢ=π₁(Vᵢ), Bᵢ=π₂(Vᵢ). Coordinate projections are 1-Lipschitz in the concatenated Euclidean metric, so diam(Aᵢ),diam(Bᵢ)≤ρᵢ≤δ. In interval-length formulas use the underlying real diameter ρᵢ; in ENNReal content sums use its canonical ENNReal coercion. Given ε>0 set ηᵢ=ε2^(−i−1)/(1+ρᵢ^s)>0, with ε,ρᵢ interpreted as real numbers. If Bᵢ is nonempty it is bounded; extend its infimum/supremum enclosure by total width ηᵢ to obtain open Jᵢ⊇Bᵢ of length ≤ρᵢ+ηᵢ. If Bᵢ is empty choose any open interval of length ηᵢ. For every t∈[0,1] and x∈E, (x,t) lies in some Vᵢ, so x∈Aᵢ and t∈Bᵢ⊆Jᵢ. Thus the Aᵢ with t∈Jᵢ cover E at scale δ. From the infimum definition C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢ1_{Jᵢ∩[0,1]}(t)ρᵢ^s pointwise on [0,1]. Put ν=volume.restrict([0,1]) on ambient Borel ℝ. For integration on all ℝ multiply the left side by 1_[0,1]; outside [0,1] both sides vanish, so the inequality holds everywhere. Every Jᵢ∩[0,1] is Borel; its indicator multiplied by ρᵢ^s is measurable and AEMeasurable for ν. The ambient mass is ν(ℝ)=volume([0,1])=ofReal(1−0)=1 by restriction and M011; hence ν is finite and ν([0,1])=1. Integrating the left side gives C_s(E,δ)ν([0,1])=C_s(E,δ), by M010 on [0,1] with constant C_s(E,δ). M009 monotonicity bounds this by the integral of the series. Apply M002 to interchange the ℕ-indexed sum and lintegral; countability and AEMeasurability were checked. M010 gives each summand integral as ρᵢ^sν(Jᵢ∩[0,1]). For S=Jᵢ∩[0,1], restriction gives ν(S)=volume(S∩[0,1])=volume(S). Enclose S in a closed interval of length at most ρᵢ+ηᵢ (if S is empty any singleton interval suffices). M013 gives volume(S)≤volume of the enclosure, and M011 evaluates that as ofReal(length)≤ofReal(ρᵢ+ηᵢ). Therefore C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+∑'ᵢηᵢρᵢ^s≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+ε, using ρᵢ^s(ρᵢ+ηᵢ)=ρᵢ^(s+1)+ηᵢρᵢ^s and ∑ᵢ2^(−i−1)=1. For this fixed cover ε is arbitrary: if its (s+1)-cost is finite, ε↓0 gives C_s(E,δ)≤that cost; if infinite the inequality is immediate. Taking the infimum over all Nat-indexed δ-covers yields C_s(E,δ)≤