lNUsxInAAc1Eu5lEYtN8LOwf9pro1iw2m9Fevn93cyeuyoqSTwlQP0RGCEeZj9ostTctgHdWIaMtb_Lv9lgT143vvBc4IWkQrUgRmqBNGoDMxH_2xCP69ZRF-7lebx6FpgSwOE7kv0NHkd-F3imn0CgbHbYk6yhN6ZT1bBq2-zqZ8ItUAGaA7_k0bAltEhFuFit33Ic4D1ynMJLP90TsCFJfmPQQE9w1n26B-MslrTcqQ5g9bEDIgrredMVOB0xREX35nqvZk3DoiQmxHqSZbZkPmiKoHsUzV7cQTk6SzPPhomqS4HnzjANMiuusXgxz_z1dTm00B9ccXkBtdItuAPbGXDehVxc9QPHlfw6OauZxjFLY-ehe4MH2SDqKq0624eRpcIo040ghJIUk1paonOezfpronZCpunUOJ62aH03Re5ehIyk7TWmf--kreZYz58gXW5ZaA8AQL4yKkSWMLd_36q1eF_XvT4eJQobn80sSH5DiHkodW09sTy8P5rCQl5CuZ1wc6-WdbAW5ruDasHLP9jvB_esQpqW_jdm9MfA1tQjU6Sv9dw5KRBHnvg-Ug934Xq1i7X2EB-7xgVzSZaZ2Q4T0DgHSvnTQBxI6w10UUQLexBK2U43VaIsYnb3nC6TcHjIW--PU1R6uFTh133uA6XYXg=="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0c17af8fc60a9be3016adb53c760d0819187a4cd3ce391955b","call_id":"call_0743e46ff2a24b948742bdce5cb22646","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":14,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"M014\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For every Borel extended metric space X, set A⊆X and d:NNReal, if Measure.hausdorffMeasure (↑d) A=⊤, then ↑d≤dimH(A).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"dim_H\",\"Hausdorff measure\"],\"source\":{\"statement\":\"For every Borel extended metric space X, set A⊆X and d:NNReal, if Measure.hausdorffMeasure (↑d) A=⊤, then ↑d≤dimH(A).\",\"hypotheses\":[\"The Hausdorff measure at NNReal exponent d equals top.\"],\"declaration\":\"le_dimH_of_hausdorffMeasure_eq_top\",\"module\":\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\"}}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/inputs/-\",\"value\":\"M014\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/uses/-\",\"value\":\"M014\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"value\":\"For D>0 fix 0<s<D. For a>0 define C_a(A,δ)=inf{∑'ᵢ ediam(Uᵢ)^a : U:ℕ→Set(X), A⊆⋃ᵢUᵢ and ∀i ediam(Uᵢ)≤δ}. Empty members have diameter zero and hence zero cost for a>0. In M008, the supremum over nonempty witnesses is the ordinary power for a nonempty member and zero for the empty member; thus its inner infimum is exactly this content and H^a(A)=sup_{δ>0}C_a(A,δ), with no normalization factor. If δ₁≤δ₂, every δ₁-admissible cover is δ₂-admissible, so C_a(A,δ₁)≥C_a(A,δ₂). The one-sided limit as scale decreases to zero therefore equals this supremum: positive scales are cofinal at zero and contents are monotone in this direction. M001 gives H^s(E)=∞; hence for every finite K all sufficiently small positive δ have C_s(E,δ)>K. Fix δ>0 and any countable δ-cover (Vᵢ) of F. Set ρᵢ=ediam(Vᵢ), Aᵢ=π₁(Vᵢ), Bᵢ=π₂(Vᵢ). Coordinate projections are 1-Lipschitz in the concatenated Euclidean metric, so diam(Aᵢ),diam(Bᵢ)≤ρᵢ≤δ. In interval-length formulas use the underlying real diameter ρᵢ; in ENNReal content sums use its canonical ENNReal coercion. Given ε>0 set ηᵢ=ε2^(−i−1)/(1+ρᵢ^s)>0, with ε,ρᵢ interpreted as real numbers. If Bᵢ is nonempty it is bounded; extend its infimum/supremum enclosure by total width ηᵢ to obtain open Jᵢ⊇Bᵢ of length ≤ρᵢ+ηᵢ. If Bᵢ is empty choose any open interval of length ηᵢ. For every t∈[0,1] and x∈E, (x,t) lies in some Vᵢ, so x∈Aᵢ and t∈Bᵢ⊆Jᵢ. Thus the Aᵢ with t∈Jᵢ cover E at scale δ. From the infimum definition C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢ1_{Jᵢ∩[0,1]}(t)ρᵢ^s pointwise on [0,1]. Put ν=volume.restrict([0,1]) on ambient Borel ℝ. For integration on all ℝ multiply the left side by 1_[0,1]; outside [0,1] both sides vanish, so the inequality holds everywhere. Every Jᵢ∩[0,1] is Borel; its indicator multiplied by ρᵢ^s is measurable and AEMeasurable for ν. The ambient mass is ν(ℝ)=volume([0,1])=ofReal(1−0)=1 by restriction and M011; hence ν is finite and ν([0,1])=1. Integrating the left side gives C_s(E,δ)ν([0,1])=C_s(E,δ), by M010 on [0,1] with constant C_s(E,δ). M009 monotonicity bounds this by the integral of the series. Apply M002 to interchange the ℕ-indexed sum and lintegral; countability and AEMeasurability were checked. M010 gives each summand integral as ρᵢ^sν(Jᵢ∩[0,1]). For S=Jᵢ∩[0,1], restriction gives ν(S)=volume(S∩[0,1])=volume(S). Enclose S in a closed interval of length at most ρᵢ+ηᵢ (if S is empty any singleton interval suffices). M013 gives volume(S)≤volume of the enclosure, and M011 evaluates that as ofReal(length)≤ofReal(ρᵢ+ηᵢ). Therefore C_s(E,δ)≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+∑'ᵢηᵢρᵢ^s≤∑'ᵢρᵢ^(s+1)+ε, using ρᵢ^s(ρᵢ+ηᵢ)=ρᵢ^(s+1)+ηᵢρᵢ^s and ∑ᵢ2^(−i−1)=1. For this fixed cover ε is arbitrary: if its (s+1)-cost is finite, ε↓0 gives C_s(E,δ)≤that cost; if infinite the inequality is immediate. Taking the infimum over all Nat-indexed δ-covers yields C_s(E,δ)≤C_(s+1)(F,δ). As δ decreases to zero the left side diverges, so the right side diverges; by M008 H^(s+1)(F)=⊤. Apply M014, the theorem that top Hausdorff measure at NNReal exponent s+1 implies that exponent is at most dim_H(F), to obtain s+1≤dim_H(F). This holds for every 0<s<D, so taking the supremum over s gives D+1≤dim_H(F). Use NNReal coercions in dimension theorems and corresponding real exponents in M008.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/12/input\",\"value\":\"M014\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/12/bindings\",\"value\":\"Instantiate le_dimH_of_hausdorffMeasure_eq_top with product ambient space, set F, and NNReal exponent coercion of s+1.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/12/hypothesis_checks/0\",\"value\":\"The preceding argument established Hausdorff measure of F at the coercion of s+1 equals top; the ambient space is extended metric, Borel and measurable.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer